        "description": "<p>Taiwanese officials have <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://www.taiwannews.com.tw/news/6281791\" data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\">issued</a> an arrest warrant for OnePlus CEO Pete Lau on allegations of illegally employing workers in Taiwan. Two Taiwanese citizens who worked for Lau have also been indicted. The China-based smartphone company has been accused of illegally recruiting more than 70 engineers from Taiwan.&nbsp;</p><p>Members of the Shilin District Prosecutors Office claim that OnePlus reportedly set up a shell company in Hong Kong with a distinct name, then launched a branch in Taiwan in 2015 without government approval. The branch reportedly worked on research and development for OnePlus mobile phones. Taiwanese officials claim these actions by OnePlus violated the <a target=\"_blank\" class=\"link\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-Strait_Act\" data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\">Cross-Strait Act</a>, which is designed as a guide for relations between Taiwan and mainland Ch",
