        "description": "<p>Apple and Google have <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.engadget.com/ai/apples-siri-ai-will-be-powered-by-gemini-153636649.html\">confirmed</a> that Gemini\u2019s models power the new version of Siri and other generative AI features. <em>CNBC</em> broke the news, but Apple and Google soon followed up with a lengthy joint statement. Here\u2019s part of it: \u201cApple determined that Google\u2019s Al technology provides the most capable foundation for Apple Foundation Models\u2026 Apple Intelligence will continue to run on Apple devices and Private Cloud Compute, while maintaining Apple\u2019s industry-leading privacy standards.\u201d</p>\n<p>In June, it was reported that Apple was considering partnerships with OpenAI and Anthropic for Siri (the voice assistant can currently tap ChatGPT for certain queries as part of Apple Intelligence). Two months later, Google emerged as a contender. Another report suggested Apple might build the new Siri using a custom version of Gemini \u2014 and that it would pay Google aro",
